"answer": "Examples of complementary and alternative medicine (CAM) therapies for cancer include acupuncture, chiropractic, and herbal medicines [MLP-3192]. Other methods mentioned involve special foods, supplements, or diets, as well as techniques focusing on breathing or body movements to promote relaxation [MLP-3192]. Additionally, meditation is cited as a relaxation method used to cope with cancer [MLP-1540]. The sources note that while some CAM therapies like acupuncture may help manage side effects such as nausea and pain, their safety and effectiveness are often still under study [MLP-3192, MLP-132]."
